I am standing in the supermarket after work.
There are many people in the store today.
I have my shopping list in my hand.
I need exact amounts for my dinner tomorrow.
First, I go over to the vegetables.
I find some small, good potatoes.
I put them in a bag and weigh them.
The scale shows exactly one kilo.
That is the right amount for the recipe.
Then, I take two large, yellow onions.
After that, I walk over to the meat.
I need minced pork for the meatballs.
I look at the different packages in the cooler.
I choose a package with five hundred grams.
Finally, I check my list one extra time.
I also take a package of butter and a little milk.
I put all the things down into my basket.
Now I am ready to cook for Kasper and Sara.
